Create a project or import a modpack archive

Usage: empack init [OPTIONS] [DIR]

Arguments:
  [DIR]  Directory for the modpack project (created if needed)

Options:
  -f, --force
          Replace existing managed project content after preparation succeeds
  -m, --modloader <MODLOADER>
          Mod loader to use (none for vanilla; skips interactive prompt) [env: EMPACK_MODLOADER=]
      --mc-version <MC_VERSION>
          Minecraft version (skips interactive prompt) [env: EMPACK_MC_VERSION=]
      --state-dir <STATE_DIR>
          Durable operation and recovery storage, separate from disposable caches [env:
          EMPACK_STATE_DIR=]
      --cache-dir <CACHE_DIR>
          Disposable cache root; previews only inspect existing objects [env: EMPACK_CACHE_DIR=]
      --java <JAVA>
          Java major for this pack, such as 21 (default: newest supported major)
  -A, --author <AUTHOR>
          Author name (skips interactive prompt) [env: EMPACK_AUTHOR=]
  -n, --pack-name <PACK_NAME>
          Modpack display name (default: directory basename) [env: EMPACK_NAME=]
      --loader-version <LOADER_VERSION>
          Loader version (skips interactive prompt) [env: EMPACK_LOADER_VERSION=]
      --pack-version <PACK_VERSION>
          Pack version (skips interactive prompt) [env: EMPACK_PACK_VERSION=]
      --datapack-folder <DATAPACK_FOLDER>
          Folder for datapacks relative to pack root [env: EMPACK_DATAPACK_FOLDER=]
      --world-folder <WORLD_FOLDER>
          Parent folder for interpreted world directories, relative to the pack root [env:
          EMPACK_WORLD_FOLDER=]
      --game-versions <GAME_VERSIONS>
          Additional accepted MC versions (comma-separated) [env: EMPACK_GAME_VERSIONS=]
      --from <SOURCE>
          Import modpack from a source (file path or URL)
  -y, --yes
          Run without prompts; unresolved content choices still fail [env: EMPACK_YES=]
      --dry-run
          Preview changes without publishing project, instance or durable state [env:
          EMPACK_DRY_RUN=]
      --import-optional-default <BOOL>
          Default for optional imported files; participation remains optional [possible values:
          true, false]
      --exclude-auxiliary
          Explicitly exclude archive members outside recognized content namespaces
      --import-local-files
          Retain imported downloads as local files instead of durable URL references
      --import-file <SELECTOR=PATH>
          Associate a selected file with one exact imported download obligation
  -h, --help
          Print help
  -V, --version
          Print version
